<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.KOREAN GROUP OF FIRMS BUY 30,000T CHINESE CORN.</title>
<headline>S.KOREAN GROUP OF FIRMS BUY 30,000T CHINESE CORN.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>A South Korean buyer group, known as the Big Feed Mills, has purchased 30,000 tonnes of Chinese corn at $124.65 a tonne, C&amp;F, traders said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>They said the purchase was made through a closed tender on Monday.</p>
<p>Shipment was slated for October 17-November 5 to the western port of Inchon.</p>
<p>They said the seller was Nidera.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5650</p>
</text>
